This project builds on two upstream PointNet++ code bases. Their terms apply to
the derived portions, which are redistributed here in modified form:

  Pointnet_Pointnet2_pytorch   - MIT License, Copyright (c) 2019 benny
                                 https://github.com/yanx27/Pointnet_Pointnet2_pytorch
                                 Origin of the set-abstraction and feature-
                                 propagation modules in models/, of the
                                 augmentation helpers in provider.py, and of the
                                 training and evaluation scaffolding.

  Pointnet2_PyTorch            - The Unlicense (public domain)
                                 https://github.com/erikwijmans/Pointnet2_PyTorch
                                 Source of the `pointnet2_ops` CUDA extension,
                                 installed as a dependency and not vendored here.

The method those modules are derived from was introduced in PointNet++ (Qi,
Yi, Su, Guibas; NeurIPS 2017).

The standalone LGD extractor under LGD/ carries its own LICENSE file,
including the terms of the header-only libraries it vendors.
